    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0342" n="324" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p1/pg324"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">790B.00/12–2051: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Burma</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Day</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rangoon</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1951-12-20T23:00:00+06:30">December 20, 1951—11 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>593. Burmese Government has granted Dr. Seagrave permission return to hospital
                    Namkham upon his written undertaking to leave the Shan State when authorities
                    there require him to do so.</p>
                <p>PermSec FonOff told me in confidence PriMin, FonMin and Home Min had to overcome strong opposition in quarters
                    not specified but believed military. Consequently believe publicity to decision
                    in Burma undesirable though desirable in US in interests Burmese American
                    relations. Seagrave should reach Namkham before Christmas.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Day</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
